WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.502
Settings: switch optional SMS assistance off then on; separately select Ask/Email/SMS bank-code delivery.

2
00:00:05.552 --> 00:00:15.502
Optional assistance uses Android consent for one message, not inbox access. Keyboard autofill still waits for Verify.

3
00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:21.957
Settings: switch optional SMS assistance off then on; separately select Ask/Email/SMS bank-code delivery.

4
00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:27.957
SMS assistance is switched off only in this settings scene, then restored on. Keyboard and manual entry remain available.

5
00:00:28.007 --> 00:00:33.549
Settings: switch optional SMS assistance off then on; separately select Ask/Email/SMS bank-code delivery.

6
00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:41.549
SMS assistance is on. Android requests per-message approval; only an approved SMS-only login auto-verifies.

7
00:00:41.599 --> 00:00:47.328
Settings: switch optional SMS assistance off then on; separately select Ask/Email/SMS bank-code delivery.

8
00:00:47.378 --> 00:00:53.328
Ask lets you choose a channel when the bank offers alternatives. It does not change Android autofill.

9
